# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Yuki Nagai et al. (2026). Target-Distribution-Guided Cross-Functional Fine-Tuning of Machine-Learning Interatomic Potentials.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2605.25032  arXiv:2605.25032v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2605.25032v1 (sha256 8d75628e882c0865...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 453 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/nagai2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the small MACE-MP-0 foundation model sequentially
# fine-tuned on self-learning hybrid Monte Carlo (SLHMC) data for 48-atom
# rutile TiO2, with target energies and forces at PBE, r2SCAN or HSE06
# (VASP), and the forward-in-time force RMSEs at the final analysed
# updates stated in the text. Nearest-neighbour distributions, RDFs and
# NPT cell parameters are properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
